          "heading": "Experimental Laboratory Investigation: Laboratory 11: Ideal-vapor dew pressure",
          "content": "# Laboratory 11: Ideal-vapor dew pressure\n\n**Model:** 1/Pdew=yA/PsatA+(1\u2212yA)/PsatB\n\n**Controllable variables:** Vapor mole fraction A (fraction) and Temperature (K).\n\n## Governing relation\n\n1/Pdew=yA/PsatA+(1\u2212yA)/PsatB. This relation is used for an educational screening calculation, not certified physical-property or process-safety design. Every output must be checked against dimensional consistency, equilibrium assumptions and an independent reference when applied to real chemicals.\n\n## Stated limitations\n\nLow-pressure ideal vapor/liquid, hypothetical species data.\n\n## Step-by-step investigation\n\n1. Record the default inputs and the readout with its units. Sketch the qualitative expected trend before inspecting the chart.\n2. Decrease **Vapor mole fraction A** to its minimum while keeping **Temperature** fixed. Record the change and explain which term in the governing equation is responsible.\n3. Increase **Vapor mole fraction A** to its maximum and compare the response with the first observation. Determine whether the dependence is linear, logarithmic, exponential or nonlinear for a reason you can explain.\n4. Reset, then alter **Temperature** and repeat. Estimate a finite-difference sensitivity between two nearby parameter values, including its units.\n5. Export the response curve to CSV. Explain how a plotted sensitivity helps select a range for a laboratory measurement or a process-control test.\n6. Identify the first physical mechanism omitted by the model that would become important if the system were pressurized, heated, mixed or scaled up substantially.\n\n## Questions\n\n**Reasoning:** Why does the dew-pressure expression use reciprocal saturation pressures?\n\n**Extension:** Compare bubble and dew pressure at numerically equal xA=yA.\n\n**Uncertainty:** How would uncertainty in temperature influence your interpretation of the response curve? Which single additional measurement would best distinguish model error from input uncertainty?\n\n## Evidence to submit\n\nExport a parameter sweep from the interactive model and attach it with your explanation of **1/Pdew=yA/PsatA+(1\u2212yA)/PsatB**. Demonstrate the predicted change in **Vapor mole fraction A** at two different settings of **Temperature**. Conclude by explaining whether the laboratory's approximation **(Low-pressure ideal vapor/liquid, hypothetical species data.)** would remain credible in a real chemical process."
